{
  "slug": "chest-tombs-of-amascut",
  "note": "Hand-authored from Chest (Tombs of Amascut) revid 15274037 and Module:Tombs of Amascut loot revid 15216862 (the Lua behind the page's own {{Calculator:Tombs of Amascut loot}}). The chest's dropsline rows are structural leftovers of a point-purchase reward shop, not per-row rarities: the unique roll is a single points-and-raid-level probability, the common table's quantities are computed from points, and the tertiary rows carry kill-count and ownership state. None of that is in any drop row, so no parser improvement reaches it. Modelled per player, solo. The module divides points and chances by team size; the page states the group unique roll uses pooled points with per-player probability proportional to contribution. One chest for one player is this simulator's unit, so team size is out of scope rather than approximated. ctx.points is the reward-point total AS USED FOR LOOT, i.e. already net of the 5,000 starting points the page says are subtracted at the end (confirmed by the cited JagexAsh tweet). The module never adds them either. NOT modelled, deliberately: the five remnant challenge rewards (need \"all <boss> invocations and level 4 <boss>\", inexpressible); the elite combat achievement's 1.05x clue multiplier (no CA context exists); duplicate jewels once all four are owned (needs conjoined ownership gates, and it is a terminal state that changes no headline figure).",
